{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-006", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "OEKO-TEX traceability gains momentum ahead of new EU rules", "content": "OEKO-TEX strengthened traceability across global textile supply chains in 2025/26, with ORGANIC COTTON certified volumes exceeding 33 million kg across more than 20 countries and certificates rising over 200 per cent.\nMADE IN GREEN demand grew over 13 per cent, while digital traceability tools and independent certification support compliance with evolving EU rules.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/oeko-tex-traceability-gains-momentum-ahead-of-new-eu-rules-313161-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-007", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s DGFT automates free sale certificates for exporters", "content": "India’s DGFT has enabled automated issuance of Free Sale and Commerce Certificates on its portal for eligible export applications. \nThe change covers items outside the Drugs & Cosmetics Act, 1940, reducing manual routing for many certificate requests. \nApplications needing checks will still go to regional authorities, with risk-based review retained for oversight. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-dgft-automates-free-sale-certificates-for-exporters-313159-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-008", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Global cotton output to slightly exceed consumption in 2026-27", "content": "Global cotton output is forecast at 26.2 million tonnes in 2026-27, just above use, though weather and pests could cut surplus. \nIndia’s crop and mill use are rising on textile export growth, while Pakistan’s weaker output will deepen raw cotton import reliance. \nChina reserve sales aid supply, but Xinjiang risks may lift imports; US acreage and Section 301 tariffs could redirect sourcing flows. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/global-cotton-output-to-slightly-exceed-consumption-in-2026-27-313155-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-009", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "order_visibility", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["improve", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "ICE cotton corrects sharply due to profit booking, stronger dollar", "content": "ICE December 2026 cotton settled at 91.55 cents, down 1.59 cent, after gaining about 13 per cent in August. \nA stronger US dollar, improved rainfall and profit-taking pressured prices, while crude oil strength failed to support cotton. \nOpen interest reached 382,071, the third-highest in cotton history; USDA rated the US crop 39 per cent Good/Excellent versus 51 per cent a year earlier. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-corrects-sharply-due-to-profit-booking-stronger-dollar-313147-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-010", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "40% FOC rule could force a new MMF capacity race in Bangladesh", "content": "Bangladesh imported $1.818 billion of selected MMF fibres, yarns and fabrics in H1 2026, up 2.34 per cent year on year.\nWoven MMF fabric made up 63.0 per cent of the basket, with China supplying 81.85 per cent.\nThe August Import Policy Order raises FOC thresholds to 40 per cent for specialised synthetic-fibre products and underwear, testing backward linkages.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/40-foc-rule-could-force-a-new-mmf-capacity-race-in-bangladesh-313143-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-02-011", "date": "2026-09-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s garment exporters go global as US apparel trade falls 25%", "content": "TexPro says India’s apparel exports fell 11.2 per cent year on year to about $7.88 billion in H1 2026, with US shipments down 24.5 per cent.\nUK, Germany, Netherlands, Spain, France and Italy raised their combined share to 34.61 per cent, though value slipped about 1.5 per cent.\nExporters are building networks across Asia, Africa and the Americas as origin optionality becomes a sourcing hedge.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-garment-exporters-go-global-as-us-apparel-trade-falls-25--313148-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
